    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0115_a7bb04e276ba.png\" style=\"width: 325px; height: 148px;\" /></p><p>In the above circuit diagram of the gate, the result of the above combination is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>A</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>, using&nbsp;Demorgan&#39;s theorem,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math>, so this circuit is equivalent&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NOR</mi></math>&nbsp;gate.</p>"
  }
